    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The apparent hERG margin is **600-fold** (30 \u00b5M / 0.05 \u00b5M), which is reassuring. I would **prioritise Compound A for the next study**, provided the IC50 and Cmax are measured on comparable free-concentration bases and there are no other liabilities.\n\nNext, test:\n\n1. **Confirm hERG** with an orthogonal assay, including concentration\u2013response quality, exposure stability, and protein-binding/free-drug correction.\n2. **Broader cardiac ion-channel profiling**, especially Nav1.5 and Cav1.2, followed by a cardiac action-potential assay.\n3. **In vivo telemetry/QT assessment** at exposures covering the intended dose and supra-therapeutic multiples, with toxicokinetic sampling.\n4. **Metabolite coverage**, ensuring major circulating metabolites are tested for hERG and cardiac effects.\n\nA high hERG IC50 alone does not establish overall cardiac safety; the priority decision should remain conditional on exposure confirmation and the broader cardiac profile.",
